WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:02.893
Microbiome discoveries are everywhere.

2
00:00:03.123 --> 00:00:03.981
How do we connect them?

3
00:00:04.391 --> 00:00:08.257
MINERVA turns over one hundred twenty-nine thousand publications

4
00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:12.286
into more than sixty-six thousand microbe-disease relationships.

5
00:00:12.668 --> 00:00:15.991
It identifies microbes and diseases in sentences.

6
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:19.741
A fine-tuned language model extracts their reported relationships.

7
00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.493
Repeated model answers must fully agree.

8
00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:24.541
Source sentences stay attached

9
00:00:24.853 --> 00:00:27.504
as evidence is combined across papers.

10
00:00:27.916 --> 00:00:30.254
In sentence-level testing, retained predictions

11
00:00:30.254 --> 00:00:33.160
reached an F-one score of point eight eight four,

12
00:00:33.402 --> 00:00:35.081
with eighty-one percent coverage.

13
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:38.073
Explore patterns, propose missing links,

14
00:00:38.176 --> 00:00:41.268
and compare microbiome profiles with healthy references.

15
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.852
These are research hypotheses, not diagnoses.

16
00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:46.958
MINERVA turns scattered findings

17
00:00:46.958 --> 00:00:49.378
into evidence you can inspect and test.
